<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zibhebhu kaMaphitha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1904</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zibhebhu kaMaphitha was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> chief of the Mandlakazi, a branch of the royal house, who fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a> of 1879. In the British settlement that followed he became one of thirteen chiefs ruling Zululand and the main rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetshwayo">Cetshwayo</a> and his heir Dinuzulu. He defeated Cetshwayo in 1883 but was beaten by Dinuzulu and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> allies in 1884.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zibhebhu-kamaphitha.jpg" alt="Zibhebhu kaMaphitha" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William A Walton · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zibhebhu_1884.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
